Proper enumeration has to be done before any exploitations. 
- Know the landscape of the target - "map" the network.
Ports - network construct for receiving connection.
	-> will be opened by any network enabled devices.
	-> helps in running multiple network services without errors 
	-> the number of ports are 0-65535 (2 to the power of 16 - 65536) 
Port scanning provides basically the mapping we need for understanding the landscape.
Standard ports are there which is 1024 in total
80 - http, 443 - https, 139 - Windows NETBIOS, 445 - SMB

Nmap is a tool that is used for portscanning widely, it is currently the industry standard one and it has a powerful functionality. Also, with its scripting Engine, vulnerability scanning can also be done.
Nmap switches - command arguments that tells the program to do different things.
Some of the switches are:
-sT - TCP Connect scan
-sS - SYN scan
-sU - UDP scan
-O - OS detection
-sV - detecting the version of the services
-v - verbosity (-vv -level 2 verbosity and so on in similar pattern)
-oA - report in 3 major format
-oN - normal format 
-oG - Grepable format
-A - aggressive mode (service detection, os detection, traceroute, common script scanning)
-T<number> (-T5 level 5 (0-5 level)) - timing template (speed of scan)
-p 80	-p 1000-1025	-p- -these are the different ways of scanning particular ports
--script - activating script library
--script=vuln - activating all scripts in the vuln category
Different types of scans
1. TCP connect scan (-sT)
SYN, SYN/ACK, ACK
checks, maps open and completes connection
if closed RST will be the response
Mostly, firewall frops any new connection with SYN flag, so receives nothing back and marked as filtered.[can be changed in the firewall settings, so that it will send RST as response]
2. SYN scan (-sS) / "Half open", "stealth"
SYN, SYN/ACK, RST(server won't try again to establish connection)
 - helps bypass old IDS looking for 3-way handshake
 - will not logged because connection not established 
 - faster than TCP scan
 - sudo permission needed in Linux
 - Unstable services put down which can disrupt any production environments
** With sudo default will be SYN scan and without sudo it will TCP scan
3. UDP scan
no connection establishment (empty raw UDP packet send)
- no response - open|filtered and double checks by sending again
- if response (very rare) - open
- if closed, ICMP packet with port unreachable message will be the response
-- more time, more difficulty, so port numbers or range should be specified.
4. 5. 6. NULL, FIN, and XMAS Scan 
malformed packets
- expects RST as response of closed 
NULL (-sN) - empty packet without any flags will be send
FIN (-sF) - packet with only FIN flag (usually for gracefully disconnecting an active connection)
XMAS (-sX) - PSH, URG, and FIN flags (while viewing the packet capture on wireshark it blinks like a Christmas tree, thus the name)
Firewall evasion is the main purpose, as there is no SYN Flag.
* windows respond with RST to any malformed packets. 

Ping sweep - sending packet to every possible IP address in the specific network to identifyactive and inactive hosts.
nmap -sn <ip> [CIDR or range of ip with (-) is allowed]
